# 07. FACT CLASSIFICATION

Every audit finding must be classified as one of:

### VERIFIED

Directly confirmed from repository evidence.

### INFERRED

Strongly indicated by repository structure but not explicitly confirmed.

### UNKNOWN

Cannot currently be determined.

### CONFLICT

Repository behavior conflicts with an approved AEGIS specification.

### MISSING

Required by architecture but absent from repository.

### EXTRA

Exists in repository but has no approved architectural purpose.

### DEPRECATED

Exists but appears intentionally superseded.

### DEAD

Appears unused or unreachable.

### DUPLICATE

Multiple implementations appear to serve the same purpose.

