# 74. AEGIS DATA REALISM RULE

Because AEGIS represents a high-stakes healthcare and biosecurity environment:

> **The interface may simulate operational scenarios for development, but simulated data and simulated behavior must never be represented as validated real-world clinical, epidemiological, or biosecurity intelligence.**

The implementation must clearly distinguish:

```text
DEMO
SIMULATION
MOCK
TEST
REAL
```

where relevant.

---

# 75. AEGIS SAFETY BOUNDARY

AEGIS is a decision-support system architecture.

It must not be represented as independently authorizing:

```text
clinical treatment
public-health intervention
pathogen release response
laboratory manipulation
security intervention
automated real-world containment
```

without explicitly approved human governance and system boundaries.

The UI may model response workflows.

The architecture must distinguish **simulation/decision support** from actual operational authority.

